Ars Magica rulebook content — Ars Magica Open License (CC-BY-SA 4.0)
===================================================================

This directory (`rules/source/`) contains the human-authored Ars Magica 5th
Edition rulebook text used as the authoritative source for this project. All of
it is covered by the terms below, and NONE of it is covered by the MIT License
that governs the project's source code (see the top-level `LICENSE` file).

These terms follow the text wherever it goes. In particular they also govern the
rules text extracted from this Markdown into the string values of
`rules/i18n/<lang>/` — the names, descriptions, summaries and specialties the
application displays. That directory is dual-licensed: its JSON *form* (schema,
key names, the slug-identifier scheme) is MIT, while the rules *text* it carries
is CC-BY-SA 4.0 under these terms. See `rules/i18n/LICENSE` for that split. The
language-neutral mechanics in `rules/core/` contain no rulebook text and are MIT
throughout — see `rules/core/LICENSE`.

